Subject: [PATCH] net/xfrm: add Kconfig entries for INET_IPSEC_OFFLOAD / INET6_IPSEC_OFFLOAD

ASK patch 040 (`ask-xfrm-ipsec-offload.patch`) gates the entire
`nlkey_socket` / NETLINK_KEY registration path in `net/key/af_key.c`
(and `ipsec_flow.[ch]` + xfrm_state byh-hash + xfrm_input/xfrm_output
offload hooks) on:

    #if defined(CONFIG_INET_IPSEC_OFFLOAD) || defined(CONFIG_INET6_IPSEC_OFFLOAD)

Neither symbol is defined as a real Kconfig option anywhere in tree or
in the patch set, so the gate is permanently `n` at preprocess time and
the NETLINK_KEY socket is never registered. Userspace `cmm` then fails
on its second `fci_open()` with EPROTONOSUPPORT and `cmm.service` does
not come up.

Add real Kconfig entries so a defconfig can opt in. The defconfig flip
is applied separately in `release/vyos-base/10-networking.config`.

Both default `n` so non-LS1046A users of this kernel are unaffected
until they explicitly enable them.

Signed-off-by: ASK fix-plan <FIX-PLAN-FCI-NETLINK-KEY.md>
---
diff --git a/net/xfrm/Kconfig b/net/xfrm/Kconfig
index 3adf31a..ba99f4f 100644
--- a/net/xfrm/Kconfig
+++ b/net/xfrm/Kconfig
@@ -11,6 +11,22 @@ config XFRM
 config XFRM_OFFLOAD
 	bool
 
+config INET_IPSEC_OFFLOAD
+	bool "IPv4 IPsec offload (NXP/ASK)"
+	depends on XFRM && INET
+	default n
+	help
+	  Enables NXP CAAM / ASK IPv4 IPsec offload control plane.
+	  Registers the NETLINK_KEY socket and the af_key.c nlkey_socket
+	  hooks consumed by the ASK userspace cmm/dpa_ipsec daemons.
+
+config INET6_IPSEC_OFFLOAD
+	bool "IPv6 IPsec offload (NXP/ASK)"
+	depends on XFRM && IPV6
+	default n
+	help
+	  IPv6 counterpart of INET_IPSEC_OFFLOAD.
+
 config XFRM_ALGO
 	tristate
 	select XFRM
